  {
   "id": 547881,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Some fish swim in schools, which can respond rapidly by moving quickly away from predator threats. In schools, fish swim in a coordinated pattern without moving chaotically and bumping into one another. Which type of communication between individuals could account for the precisely coordinated movements of all of the fish in a school in response to a threat?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1075651,
     "content_html": "aural signals"
    },
    {
     "id": 1075652,
     "content_html": "pheromone signals"
    },
    {
     "id": 1075653,
     "content_html": "tactile signals"
    },
    {
     "id": 1075654,
     "content_html": "visual signals"
    }
   ],
